]7. How do you a)bless items (any way other than through enchant
]armor.weapon scrolls) b)wish for specific items (like Stormbringer
]etc.), and c)should you #pray only when you need stuff, or every (I
]think its 1000) turns.
	Some characters just *know* about blessings and curses.
	Other characters have to ask the gods.
	Wishing for an object is a rare gift, so be careful to ask
	for exactly what you want to have, and don't get greedy and
	ask for more than three of anything at once.
	Enlightenment is a blessing, and a blessed spellbook of identify
	can teach you a lot, but different people desire different things -
	maybe you'd be happier with a +3 two-handed sword, or 
	some black dragon scale armor, or a ring of conflict.
	Sometimes all you want is a couple tins of spinach.
	In olden times, some brazen adventurers would wish for wands
	of wishing, but these days that would be considered greedy.

	Do the gods enourage prayer?  Of course they do, if the
	motivation is to know them better, rather than greed.
	Sometimes you can gain new insights!  Sometimes they'll help
	you when you're in serious trouble.  In earlier ages of the
	world, the moral standard for greed was rigid - always wait 300 turns.
	The current gods are more complex; sometimes the wait is
	shorter, but often longer.  (The source code looks UGLY here!)
	What would you do to appease them?

